            <title>[LU-21139] conf-sanity test_153c: class_decref_free() ASSERTION OBDF_ATTACHED at MDT umount, obd_zombid</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21139</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;conf-sanity test_153c crashed the MDS node (trevis-154vm347, el10.2 ldiskfs, review-dne-part-3, kernel 6.12.0-211.47.1.el10_2_lustre) during cleanup, at the umount of lustre-MDT0001:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LustreError: (obd_config.c:1092:class_decref_free()) ASSERTION( !test_bit(OBDF_ATTACHED, obd-&amp;gt;obd_flags) ) failed&lt;br/&gt;
LustreError: (obd_config.c:1092:class_decref_free()) LBUG&lt;br/&gt;
Workqueue: obd_zombid obd_zombie_imp_cull &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;obdclass&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
  class_decref_free+0x98/0xa0 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;obdclass&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
  obd_zombie_import_free+0x249/0x5b0 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;obdclass&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
  process_one_work, worker_thread, kthread&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Timeline from the console log: test 153c starts at 40992 s; at 41009 s "lustre-MDT0000-osp-MDT0001: Connection to lustre-MDT0000 was lost"; the test calls cleanup, "umount -d -f /mnt/lustre-mds2" at 41014 s; the zombie import worker hits the assertion at 41020 s. An obd's refcount reached zero while the device was still attached, when the zombie worker freed an import: a refcount imbalance or an obd detached too late on the server umount path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen once in review-dne-part-3: 0 failures of this group in 1362 review runs over the previous 30 days, and 6 of 6 other runs of this change passed. The change under test (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20690" title="FLR-EC: handle '--ec k+p' components with p &amp;gt; k" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20690"&gt;LU-20690&lt;/a&gt; EC, lod, lfs and tests) does not touch obdclass, ptlrpc or osp. The only other recent test_153c crash (change 70378, 2026-11-05) is an LNet lnet_assert_handler_unused assertion, a different failure, already linked to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20842" title="LNet: Peer discovery ping/push concurrency ref leak" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20842"&gt;LU-20842&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/bf5abacc-44ae-4650-8c24-3d6361a8fdde" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/bf5abacc-44ae-4650-8c24-3d6361a8fdde&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test log for the subtest: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/568150c9-c6a8-4d6d-9885-805e0afa10bb" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/568150c9-c6a8-4d6d-9885-805e0afa10bb&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Tested change: &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69703" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69703&lt;/a&gt; patchset 7&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69703-ps7-72e2573f2e89 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69703" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69703&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
